  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Capacity Building Catholic Eparchy Secretariat Keren (CESK) Eritrea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Keren Eparchy runs many socio-pastoral services both in Anseba and Northern Red Sea regions. The services include pastoral care, education, health, women&#x2019;s development activities, water programmes, emergency programmes, social communication activities and others. Personnel engaged in delivery of these services play a crucial role in their successful delivery. The challenge is to implement the programmes with greater vigour and insight so as to achieve the intended results. This project focuses on some core areas of CESK capacity development. To main purpose of the project is to improve CESK&#x2019;s ability to fulfil its mission through inventions of transparent and accountable environment by strengthening its working systems and operations.</narrative>
  </description>
